-## QA Rules
-
-Always check:
-
-- Cells are fixed-size and aligned.
-- The baseline line matches expected foot/ground contact for standing frames.
-- The center line is stable unless the action intentionally shifts.
-- Alpha is hard and clean.
-- Color count is controlled.
-- The GIF reads as an action, not just unrelated poses.
-- The report warnings are meaningful for the animation type.
-
-For death/fall, do not fail prone frames solely because vertical body height is low. Validate phase:
-
-- early frames: standing height roughly `40-48px`;
-- middle frames: height may decrease while width increases;
-- final frames: prone shape can be about `14-34px` high and wide across the cell.
-
-For formal character animation, also require:
-
-- limbs are anchored through a plausible shoulder/elbow/wrist or hip/knee/ankle chain;
-- hands do not float in front of the chest when they should be attached to shoulders;
-- legs do not detach from the pelvis;
-- foot contact frames land near the baseline;
-- onion-skin cleanup has been completed in Aseprite;
-- PixelOver or equivalent rig files/exports exist for complex motion.
-
-For video-derived gait loops, also require:
-
-- the final 8 frames cover one complete stride cycle;
-- no duplicate or near-identical contact frames unless used intentionally as loop boundary;
-- the character does not drift across the cell after anchor locking;
-- direction is consistent in every frame;
-- approved frames are not regenerated when only later frames fail;
-- the source video segment is archived with the processed strip/GIF/QA output.
